{"cuisine/guna-foodways":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/guna-foodways","n":"Guna foodways","c":"#94bd5c","crumb":[["The Americas","cuisines#the-americas"],["Native American cuisine","cuisine/native-american-cuisine"]],"sub":"Indigenous foodways, Guna Yala, Caribbean coast and islands of Panama","names":"Guna, Dule","intro":[["On the islands of Guna Yala, off Panama's Caribbean coast, meals center on the sea. Tule masi is a soup of fish and ",["plantain","ingredient/plantain-cooking"],", fish caught the same day comes with coconut rice, and coconut water is drunk from a nut cut from the palm just before."],["Fish is still a daily food for many island families, and many have ",["cacao","ingredient/theobroma-cacao"]," every day, though researchers working on Ustupu and Ogobsucum found fried and packaged foods spreading fast. At big festivals, women stir huge pots of ",["Chicha","dish/chicha"]," made from sugarcane juice, herbs and corn."]],"src":"note","sources":[{"name":"Visit Panamá, Guna Dule community","url":"https://www.tourismpanama.com/things-to-do/indigenous-communities/guna/"},{"name":"Nutrition Journal, Examination of dietary habits among the Indigenous Kuna Indians of Panama (2019)","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6670206"},{"name":"William Benton Museum of Art, University of Connecticut, Guna culture","url":"https://benton.uconn.edu/guna-culture/"}],"actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"guna-foodways"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":1,"links":[["Chicha","dish/chicha"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Native American cuisine","cuisine/native-american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Cassava","ingredient/cassava"],["Maize","ingredient/maize"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Native American cuisine","cuisine/native-american-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Cuisine of the Americas","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/1/17/Chicha_with_Pipe%C3%B1o.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"simenon simenon","lic"