a subspecies of subtropical evergreen tree in the family Oleaceae. Modern cultivars are traced primarily to the Near East, Aegean Sea, and Strait of Gibraltar. Olea europaea is the type species for its genus, Olea, which lends its name to the Oleaceae plant family. The olive fruit is classed botanically as a drupe, similar in structure and function to the cherry or peach. The term oil was originally synonymous with olive oil."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-olive"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olive"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":8,"groups":[["Portuguese cuisine","cuisine/portuguese-cuisine",[["Bacalhau à Gomes de Sá","dish/bacalhau-a-gomes-de-sa"],["Bacalhau à minhota","dish/bacalhau-a-minhota"],["Bacalhau à Narcisa","dish/bacalhau-a-narcisa"],["Bacalhau à Zé do Pipo","dish/bacalhau-a-ze-do-pipo"],["Polvo à lagareiro","dish/polvo-a-lagareiro"]]],["Basque cuisine","cuisine/basque-cuisine",[["Gilda (snack)","dish/gilda-snack"]]],["Belarusian cuisine","cuisine/belarusian-cuisine",[["Solyanka","dish/solyanka"]]],["Greek cuisine","cuisine/greek-cuisine",[["Greek salad","dish/greek-salad"]]],["Israeli cuisine","cuisine/israeli-cuisine",[["Ziva (dish)","dish/ziva-dish"]]],["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine",[["Solyanka","dish/solyanka"]]],["Soviet cuisine","cuisine/soviet-cuisine",[["Solyanka","dish/solyanka"]]],["Ukrainian cuisine","cuisine/ukrainian-cuisine",[["Solyanka","dish/solyanka"]]]]},{"h":"Where it's grown","grown":{"what":"Olives","years":"2020 to 2024","url":"https://www.fao.org/faostat/en/#data/QCL","world":22983322,"top":[["Spain","cuisine/spanish-cuisine",6749138],["Greece","cuisine/greek-cuisine",2951088],["Italy","cuisine/italian-cuisine",2267144],["Turkey","cuisine/turkish-cuisine",2260261],["Morocco","cuisine/moroccan-cuisine",1407160],["Tunisia","cuisine/tunisian-cuisine",1209938],["Egypt","cuisine/egyptian-cuisine",1098277],["Portugal","cuisine/portuguese-cuisine"