n":"Triticum","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Wheat is a group of wild and domesticated grasses of the genus Triticum (). As cereals, they are cultivated for their grains, which are staple foods around the world. Well-known wheat species and hybrids include the most widely grown common wheat (T. aestivum), spelt, durum, emmer, einkorn, and Khorasan or Kamut. The archaeological record suggests that wheat was first cultivated in the regions of the Fertile Crescent around 9600 BC."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-triticum"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triticum"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Armenian cuisine","cuisine/armenian-cuisine",[["Spas (soup)","dish/spas-soup"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Coriander","ingredient/coriander"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Egg yolk","ingredient/egg-yolk"],["Matzoon","ingredient/matzoon"],["Parsley","ingredient/parsley"],["Wheat berry","ingredient/wheat-berry"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/a3/Vehn%C3%A4pelto_6.jpg/500px-Vehn%C3%A4pelto_6.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"kallerna","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vehn%C3%A4pelto_6.jpg"}},"dish/piib":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/piib","n":"Pib","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Maya cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["A big filled corn dough dish, also called mucbipollo, wrapped in banana leaves and buried for hours in an earth oven of fire-heated stones. ",["Maya","cuisine/maya-cuisine"]," families in Yucatán make it for Hanal Pixán, and the first pib out of the ground goes on the altar for relatives who have died."]],"src":"note","sources":[{"name":"Uno TV, El pib, la tradición yucateca que se cocina bajo tierra","url":"https://www.unotv.com/estados/yucatan/el-pib-la-tradicion-yucateca-que-se-cocina-bajo-tierra/"}],"actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-piib"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/P%C3%ADib"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Maya cuisine","cuisine/maya-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Banana leaf","ingredient/banana-leaf"],["Masa","ingredient/masa"]]},{"h":"More from Maya cuisine","links":[["Cochinita pibil","dish/cochinita-pibil"],["Kak'ik","dish/kak-ik"],["Tamale","dish/tamale"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/9/9c/Enterrando_los_pibipollos.jpg/500px-Enterrando_los_pibipollos.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Elsabordecampeche","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Enterrando_los_pibipollos.jpg"}}}